-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Yomitan
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The deinflection rule set vendored at src/common/resources/japanese-transforms.json
and the transformer in src/common/deinflect.ts are ported from Yomitan's Japanese
language transforms (ext/js/language/ja/japanese-transforms.js) and its
LanguageTransformer, by way of daidai's Ruby port.

The lookup pipeline in src/common/offline-dictionary.ts also follows Yomitan:
`collapseEmphatic` ports collapseEmphaticSequences and `katakanaToHiragana`
follows convertKatakanaToHiragana (ext/js/language/ja/japanese.js); the
part-of-speech gate on deinflected candidates (`posSatisfiesInflection`) and the
ranking tiebreakers in `contextualCompare`, prefer the most literal spelling,
then the shortest inflection chain, follow Translator's conditionsMatch check
and _sortTermDictionaryEntries (ext/js/language/translator.js).

    Yomitan: https://github.com/yomidevs/yomitan
